  "x10_report": "eval/results/x10-report-m5-b4d-midwrite.json",
  "x10_scope": [
    "B4D"
  ],
  "tests": "eval/tests/test_b4d_slice.py::B4DFixtureTests, ::B4DBackupRestoreTests, ::B4DRetryRestoreTests, ::B4DFaultInjectionTests, ::B4DCorruptBackupTests, ::B4DWriteStateModelTests, ::B4DMidWriteTests",
  "test_counts": {
    "b4d_slice_tests": 208,
    "new_tests_this_extension": 48,
    "new_state_machine_tests": 10,
    "new_mid_write_tests": 38,
    "whole_suite": 369
  },
  "harness_tests": "python3 -m unittest discover -s eval/tests -t . -> 369 tests OK; python3 -m eval.harness selftest -> 17/17 checks passed; python3 -m eval.harness x10 --block B4D -> 17/17 regressions caught by their declared gate",
  "solver_note": "Every run uses the deterministic hand-written 'stub' reference profile. No model, provider, parameter count, hardware or network call is involved. The evaluator chooses where an attempt stops and whether the retry resumes or rolls back; the reference program is told the policy (it has to follow it) and nothing about the chosen boundary, the candidate set or the gold state.",
  "what_this_shows": [
    "an attempt can be interrupted after some of a record's copies are written, and the store then holds a record that is neither absent nor complete; the four-state model names that state and the audit reports it per record, not as a count",
    "both legal recoveries work: under 'resume' the retry keeps the parts already there and finishes them, under 'rollback' it removes the record from every copy first, and the two policies reach the same final store for the same chosen point (asserted by test, not by inspection)",
    "an injected interruption fails nothing on its own: every mid-write task reports two attempts, the first incomplete, and still passes all gates when the retry recovers",
    "the three new regressions are isolated: replay_partial_write_twice fails only restore_idempotency_zero, claim_rollback_without_reverting only restore_rollback_zero, report_success_with_partial_record only restore_partial_write_zero, each at the exact tasks it damages and with the other new counters at zero",
    "the fewer-than-expected directions are covered too: a retry that never finishes the restore fails restore_recovery_zero while its rollback and idempotency counters stay clean",
    "the fixture cannot encode the answer: it declares candidate points and the loader recomputes the gold write states from the schedule and the policy, refusing the fixture when they disagree",
    "the schedule is hidden from the solver: the view carries the recovery policy and nothing about the chosen point, the candidate list, the per-record states or the gold outcome",
    "malformed reports fail closed rather than crashing the scorer: an illegal transition, an unknown write part, a non-list or missing write log and an impossible chain are all counted as rollback errors with the task failing"
  ],
  "what_this_does_not_show": [
    "that anything is durable: the stop lands between two copy writes in an in-memory simulator, no write is torn at byte level, nothing is fsynced, and there is no journal, WAL, power-failure or restart path",
    "how a real engine recovers: resume and rollback are two written policies the reference program follows, not observations of a real store's crash recovery",
    "any rate: 27 scenarios with 5 mid-write stops over 9 candidate boundaries are deterministic executions, not samples, and no confidence interval may be computed from them",
    "any product capability: the store is invented, the solver is a hand-written program, C-02-AC3 stays slice_built, no capability is marked implemented or validated, and G-O1 stays blocked",
    "real retention, legal hold, off-site replication or concurrent restores"
  ],
  "correlated_failures": [
    "three older restore mutants also trip the two new gates on the new scenarios, because they mishandle partially applied records as well: retry_from_scratch, abandon_partial_restore and falsely_claim_restore_complete report rollback errors, and the latter two also leave partial residue. That is real damage on those tasks, not leakage between gates: each mutant is still caught by its declared gate, and the three new mutants trip only their own.",
    "false_successes_zero and success_drop fire alongside every expected gate; they are aggregate companions rather than family-specific signals and are not used to argue isolation"
  ],
  "remaining_gaps": [
    "no durability or crash semantics: the four states are the simulator's, not a store's",
    "no concurrency: one restore at a time, and no interleaving with live writes",
    "mid-write interruptions are only offered on records the live store lost; a partially applied write to a record that is still present is unobservable in this simulator by construction",
    "no model is involved, so nothing here measures how a real agent or engine would behave after a partial write",
    "Q18 (people-database fields) stays open; real retention and legal-hold policy are untouched"
  ],
  "reproduce": [
    "python3 -m unittest discover -s eval/tests -t .",
    "python3 -m eval.harness selftest",
    "python3 -m eval.harness run --block B4D",
    "python3 -m eval.harness x10 --block B4D --report eval/results/x10-report-m5-b4d-midwrite.json",
    "python3 -m eval.harness baseline-freeze --block B4D --partial --name baseline-m5-b4d-midwrite.json --note '27-task B4D suite (2026-Q4.1-m5.6)'"
  ]
